	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Type `l` followed by anything. The first row logs it; the rows below are the records that match, newest first. ↩ opens a record's file, ⇧↩ copies its text, ⌥↩ moves it to the Trash, ⌘↩ renames it. The hotkey object opens the same list; set its combination (HYPER+L is a good one) by double-clicking it. `l ? &lt;question&gt;` asks a local model about the log once Model server is set or Apple Intelligence is ticked; the answer streams into a Text View, ↩ there copies it, ⌥↩ keeps it as a file and opens it.

Records are markdown files in the Log folder, one per line; their creation time is the file's creation time.</string>
